<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Than Shwe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1933">1933</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Than Shwe is a Myanmar general who led the country's military government from 1992 to 2011 as chairman of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/state-law-and-order-restoration-council">State Law and Order Restoration Council</a> and its successor, the State Peace and Development Council. He kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aung-san-suu-kyi">Aung San Suu Kyi</a> under house arrest, crushed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saffron-revolution">Saffron Revolution</a> of 2007 and moved the capital to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naypyidaw">Naypyidaw</a>, before handing power to a nominally civilian government under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thein-sein">Thein Sein</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/than-shwe.jpg" alt="Than Shwe" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of Thailand · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Than_Shwe_2010-10-11_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
